N5D4 for IDA Pro

This is an independent IDA Pro port of N5D4, the Ghidra implementation of
Neurosymbolic Disassembly by Zhaoqi Xiao.

Original project: https://github.com/gdjs2/N5D4
Source revision: 4550b15f7332398e1a9a68622f4efdee9a80fccb
Original N5D4 copyright: Copyright 2026 Zhaoqi Xiao
Original license: BSD 3-Clause. The full notice and disclaimer are in LICENSE.

Port-specific work includes IDAPython block extraction, feature mapping,
control-flow analysis, preview and undoable IDB updates, an external training
worker, and IDA benchmarking.

Research paper: Zhaoqi Xiao, Yeqi Fu, Lambang Akbar Wijayadi, Zhenkai Liang,
and Heng Yin. Neurosymbolic Disassembly. ACM CCS 2026.
https://doi.org/10.1145/3830454.3832592

Evaluation configuration and original Ghidra evaluators:
https://github.com/gdjs2/NSDA/tree/21814efab2155dab48c74eb06e43deb6b24a4970
Prebuilt GNU Coreutils binaries and ground-truth labels:
https://github.com/gdjs2/NSDA-coreutils-dataset/tree/9962bca2c5073e4ddac09a7941479f526597c36d
Those repositories retain their own notices. The benchmark report identifies
measurements produced by this port and values reported by the paper's authors.
